{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we start by determining the total number of members in the band. The band initially forms a rectangle with dimensions \\(n-2\\) and \\(n+8\\), so the total number of members is \\((n-2)(n+8)\\).\n\nIn the second stage, the band re-arranges to form a rectangle with dimensions \\(n\\) and \\(2n-3\\), excluding all the drummers. Let the number of drummers be \\(d\\). Then the number of members in the second formation is \\((n-2)(n+8) - d\\). This number of members can also be expressed as \\(n(2n-3)\\). Therefore, we have the equation:\n\\[\n(n-2)(n+8) - d = n(2n-3)\n\\]\nRearranging terms, we get:\n\\[\nn^2 + 6n - 16 - d = 2n^2 - 3n\n\\]\n\\[\n-d = n^2 - 9n + 16\n\\]\n\\[\nd = 9n - n^2 - 16\n\\]\nSince \\(d\\) is the number of drummers and is at least 4, we have:\n\\[\n9n - n^2 - 16 \\geq 4\n\\]\n\\[\n-n^2 + 9n - 20 \\geq 0\n\\]\n\\[\nn^2 - 9n + 20 \\leq 0\n\\]\nWe solve the quadratic equation \\(n^2 - 9n + 20 = 0\\) to find the roots:\n\\[\nn = \\frac{9 \\pm \\sqrt{81 - 80}}{2} = \\frac{9 \\pm 1}{2}\n\\]\n\\[\nn = 5 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad n = 4\n\\]\nThe quadratic \\(n^2 - 9n + 20 \\leq 0\\) holds for \\(4 \\leq n \\leq 5\\). We need to check these values of \\(n\\) to ensure they satisfy the conditions of the problem.\n\n","prefix_end":1172,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1191,553,25597,279,2790,1372,315,3613,304,279,7055,13,576,7055,15102,7586,264,22756,448,15336,17767,77,12,17,57758,323,17767,77,10,23,59,701,773,279,2790,1372,315,3613,374,1124,1188,77,12,17,2376,77,10,23,10699,3593,641,279,2086,6430,11,279,7055,312,12,1118,5520,311,1352,264,22756,448,15336,17767,77,57758,323,17767,17,77,12,18,59,701,43778,678,279,23196,22780,13,6771,279,1372,315,23196,22780,387,17767,67,59,568,5005,279,1372,315,3613,304,279,2086,18003,374,1124,1188,77,12,17,2376,77,10,23,8,